# Mandatory DGX → Surface sync (NO EXCEPTIONS)

Editing only on DGX leaves Surface (browser / Galaxy / commits) stale. That caused white screens, missing defaults, and commit drift.

## After ANY edit on DGX

| What changed | Required command (agent runs it — never ask the user) |
|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| `OpenNexus3DStudio/src/**` (incl. **gitignored `src/moat/`**) | `cd /home/sifr/OpenNexus3DStudio && bash scripts/sync-changes-to-pc.sh --include-src --retry-until-complete` |
| OpenNexus docs/scripts/rules (no src) | `bash scripts/sync-changes-to-pc.sh --retry-until-complete` |
| `chat/app/src/**` Companion overlay | SCP those files to `Surface:…/chat/…` **or** dedicated companion sync — do **not** use `sync-companion-to-surface.sh` if it does `git checkout -f` |
| memory-bank / agent context | add `--include-agent-context` |

## Done means synced

- Do **not** tell the user a fix is ready until the sync command has **succeeded**.
- Ad-hoc single-file `scp` is OK for hotfixes **only if** you immediately also run `sync-changes-to-pc.sh --include-src` so commits/Surface stay aligned.
- Do **not** open a new Studio browser tab after sync — hard-refresh existing `:3000/` tab.

## Why `--include-src`

`src/moat/` is **gitignored**. Incremental sync without `--include-src` **skips** live Companion/OpenNexus moat files. Always use `--include-src` after moat or any `src/` edit.

See: `OpenNexus3DStudio/.cursor/rules/dgx-sync-reminder.mdc`, `agent-run-instructions.mdc`.
